(3977927, 563218, 68769, '<td valign="top">Jeb, one advantage of having a LCD screen, is when I look at a submitted photo on my screen I can look at it from different directions and get lighter and darker images strait on yours seems a little dark and with a slight yellow cast, but when viewed looking down on my screen I see it as you probably saw it, and it is a very good picture, you might want to calibrate your monitor. In my humble opinion.</td>', 'Jeb, one advantage of having a LCD screen, is when I look at a submitted photo on my screen I can look at it from different directions and get lighter and darker images strait on yours seems a little dark and with a slight yellow cast, but when viewed looking down on my screen I see it as you probably saw it, and it is a very good picture, you might want to calibrate your monitor. In my humble opinion.', '2007-08-07 19:10:22.000000', NULL, 0),
