(3982748, 562306, 53278, '<td valign="top">greetings from the critique club,<br/> <br/>let me first by saying Dex the quality the D200 is producing is sensational!<br/> <br/>technically this shot has nothing wrong with it , the colors are vivid, good focus, composition...<br/> <br/>but i feel that the reason why the people voted it down (In my opinion) was the following,<br/>1) black and white conversion, usually street photography correlates with BW, i don''t think so personally but a lot of people do.<br/>2) there is no clear story to what to the man is doing, and this is the hear of street photography.<br/> <br/>nevertheless, the quality of the pic is quite impressive.<br/> <br/>hopefully that was helpfull!<br/>GO team D50!<br/> <br/>cheers</td>', 'greetings from the critique club, let me first by saying Dex the quality the D200 is producing is sensational! technically this shot has nothing wrong with it , the colors are vivid, good focus, composition... but i feel that the reason why the people voted it down (In my opinion) was the following,1) black and white conversion, usually street photography correlates with BW, i don''t think so personally but a lot of people do.2) there is no clear story to what to the man is doing, and this is the hear of street photography. nevertheless, the quality of the pic is quite impressive. hopefully that was helpfull!GO team D50! cheers', '2007-08-09 00:42:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983031, 562771, 38127, '<td valign="top">Nicely done!! :)</td>', 'Nicely done!! :)', '2007-08-09 03:24:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983706, 562977, 27482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club :)<br/> <br/>Sorry but this is going to be a bit short, I don´t really have much to say about the image.  It meets the challenge in my opinion, no doubt.  <br/> <br/>However, it´s pretty dark, too dark for my taste and there is well frankly not really something in the photograph that is interesting.  Sure, there are people walking there but this is just another shopping street to me.  I would vote this a 4 for those reasons.  It´s not really a bad photograph but compared to the majority of the entries in this challenge, it simply doesn´t impress me.<br/> <br/>Try using a longer shutter next time and use the histogram for metering, what you see on the back off the camera screen in nightshots can often be very misleading.  Also I find it much better to take nightshots in the city not really by night but rather around sunset or sunrise, you have then an hour or half an hour window where you still have a hint of light in the sky and that often makes a very big difference.<br/> <br/>Kind regards from Iceland, Lárus.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club :) Sorry but this is going to be a bit short, I don´t really have much to say about the image.  It meets the challenge in my opinion, no doubt.   However, it´s pretty dark, too dark for my taste and there is well frankly not really something in the photograph that is interesting.  Sure, there are people walking there but this is just another shopping street to me.  I would vote this a 4 for those reasons.  It´s not really a bad photograph but compared to the majority of the entries in this challenge, it simply doesn´t impress me. Try using a longer shutter next time and use the histogram for metering, what you see on the back off the camera screen in nightshots can often be very misleading.  Also I find it much better to take nightshots in the city not really by night but rather around sunset or sunrise, you have then an hour or half an hour window where you still have a hint of light in the sky and that often makes a very big difference. Kind regards from Iceland, Lárus.', '2007-08-09 11:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983741, 562100, 27482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club :)<br/> <br/>Well an image from Iceland!  Cool!  I don´t have a lot to say about this image so I´ll keep this short.  First of all, I am not really surprised this shot didn´t do better cause I and probably heaps of other people are wondering how it ties in with the challenge as it appears to me that it´s taken out in the nature and nowhere near a street.  It´s more what I would call a portrait.<br/> <br/>The photo itself is pretty good, I actually like it except for the sky, I don´t mind blown highlights but in this photograph, I would have liked it much better had the sky been dark and gloomy to fit the feel of the shot much better.  I do like the processing, maybe a tad too contrasty for my taste but nothing that is bothering me.  I do like the b/w conversion and the toning of the image, nicely done.<br/> <br/>Why only 513 pixles though?  You have been here for more than 2 years and almost 200 challenges, surely you know that you will score better if you stay as close to the maximum allowed pixles as you can.<br/> <br/>Anyway, nice shot, just don´t think it was in the right challenge, if it had been and also had been in a bigger rez, I think this would have easily gone over 6.<br/> <br/>Kind regards from your own Iceland, Lárus.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club :) Well an image from Iceland!  Cool!  I don´t have a lot to say about this image so I´ll keep this short.  First of all, I am not really surprised this shot didn´t do better cause I and probably heaps of other people are wondering how it ties in with the challenge as it appears to me that it´s taken out in the nature and nowhere near a street.  It´s more what I would call a portrait. The photo itself is pretty good, I actually like it except for the sky, I don´t mind blown highlights but in this photograph, I would have liked it much better had the sky been dark and gloomy to fit the feel of the shot much better.  I do like the processing, maybe a tad too contrasty for my taste but nothing that is bothering me.  I do like the b/w conversion and the toning of the image, nicely done. Why only 513 pixles though?  You have been here for more than 2 years and almost 200 challenges, surely you know that you will score better if you stay as close to the maximum allowed pixles as you can. Anyway, nice shot, just don´t think it was in the right challenge, if it had been and also had been in a bigger rez, I think this would have easily gone over 6. Kind regards from your own Iceland, Lárus.', '2007-08-09 11:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983864, 560039, 29011, '<td valign="top">Sure gives one to think about, the little things, the simple joys, they are so precious. Sometimes we just don''t see it till it''s taken away. This lady shows us we still must try to enjoy the little things in life no matter how hard life becomes or what it throws at us. Congrats on making the top10!</td>', 'Sure gives one to think about, the little things, the simple joys, they are so precious. Sometimes we just don''t see it till it''s taken away. This lady shows us we still must try to enjoy the little things in life no matter how hard life becomes or what it throws at us. Congrats on making the top10!', '2007-08-09 12:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3983881, 562758, 53278, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club,<br/> <br/>let me first say this, once a picture hits the 6 domain, it means it''a great shot.<br/> <br/>this is a great outtake on the challenge, the fact that there is no streets, YET it''s a street photography shot due to the fact that this is what they use in vietnam gave you an edge over the rest of the shots in the challenge.<br/> <br/>technically speaking the picture is very well composed, good focus with vibrant colours, so there is nothing i can tell you about this except great job.<br/> <br/>as for the shot itself, i think you could have pushed your score by at least 0.5 if:<br/>1) the shot was in BW, (for me i think it does not matter) but from what i''ve noticed for DPC masses street photog=BW, just check the top 3:)<br/> <br/>2) the story you are conveying, some shots in this challenge are good and don''t have a story (which is what street photog, is all about). yours does, it conveys the living style of some of the vietnamese communities, but it does not leave a mark on the viewer. for example if you look at the winner, it really gets to you the contrast of lifestyle shown in it, and it makes you wonder. looking at your shot,as a DPC voter, yes i see the message , cool lifestyle, votes 6 and move on.<br/> <br/>i hope this critique was helpfull,<br/>you have a good portfolio, looking forward to seing more of your work,<br/> <br/>cheers,<br/>Hassan</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club, let me first say this, once a picture hits the 6 domain, it means it''a great shot. this is a great outtake on the challenge, the fact that there is no streets, YET it''s a street photography shot due to the fact that this is what they use in vietnam gave you an edge over the rest of the shots in the challenge. technically speaking the picture is very well composed, good focus with vibrant colours, so there is nothing i can tell you about this except great job. as for the shot itself, i think you could have pushed your score by at least 0.5 if:1) the shot was in BW, (for me i think it does not matter) but from what i''ve noticed for DPC masses street photog=BW, just check the top 3:) 2) the story you are conveying, some shots in this challenge are good and don''t have a story (which is what street photog, is all about). yours does, it conveys the living style of some of the vietnamese communities, but it does not leave a mark on the viewer. for example if you look at the winner, it really gets to you the contrast of lifestyle shown in it, and it makes you wonder. looking at your shot,as a DPC voter, yes i see the message , cool lifestyle, votes 6 and move on. i hope this critique was helpfull,you have a good portfolio, looking forward to seing more of your work, cheers,Hassan', '2007-08-09 12:28:46.000000', NULL, 0),
